// Renode platform description for NXP LPC1768/LPC1769 (Cortex-M3).
//
// Renode upstream has no LPC176x platform; lpc2294.repl is the only
// LPC entry and it's the older ARM7 LPC2000 series, unrelated. No
// LPC176x-specific peripheral models exist in renode-infrastructure
// (search:repo:renode/renode-infrastructure LPC17 returns 0 hits).
//
// This file stands the platform up from scratch with what klipper
// LPC176x firmware drives at boot:
//
//   - cpu (cortex-m3) + nvic + dwt @ 100MHz (CONFIG_CLOCK_FREQ for
//     MACH_LPC1768; LPC1769 builds run faster but timer_read_time
//     just needs monotonically increasing values from DWT->CYCCNT,
//     not a precise frequency match).
//   - flash (Memory.MappedMemory @ 0x0 size 512KB) - klipper LPC
//     links at CONFIG_FLASH_APPLICATION_ADDRESS=0 (the default,
//     when LPC_FLASH_START_0000 is selected) or 0x4000 (with
//     LPC_FLASH_START_4000). Either way the ELF segments fit in
//     the first 512KB. No boot mirror needed - the LPC reset
//     vector lives in flash at 0x0 directly (no boot ROM remapping
//     like SAM3X/SAM4).
//   - sram (Memory.MappedMemory @ 0x10000000 size 32KB) - main
//     SRAM. The LPC176x AHB SRAMs (LPC_AHB_BASE 0x50000000) are
//     also present on real silicon but klipper firmware doesn't
//     use them.
//   - LPC_SC @ 0x400FC000 (size 0x200) backed by lpc_sc_stub.py.
//     Synthesizes SCS.OSCSTAT, PLL0STAT.PLOCK/PLLE/PLLC,
//     PLL1STAT.PLOCK/PLLE/PLLC; all other registers (FLASHCFG,
//     PLL0CFG, PLL0FEED, PCONP, CLKSRCSEL, CCLKCFG, PCLKSEL0/1)
//     are plain store/return. Without this SystemInit's
//     `while ((SCS & (1<<6)) == 0)` and the two PLL0STAT busy-
//     waits never complete.
//   - uart0 (UART.NS16550, wideRegisters: true) @ 0x4000C000 ->
//     nvic@5. Klipper uses LPC UART0 on P0.3/P0.2 in
//     LPC_SERIAL_UART0_P03_P02 mode (src/lpc176x/serial.c,
//     UART0_IRQn=5 per LPC1768 vector table). LPC176x UART
//     register set is classic 16550 (RBR/THR + DLL/DLM with DLAB,
//     LCR, FCR, IER, IIR, LSR); NS16550 with wideRegisters=true
//     handles the 32-bit-spaced layout.
//
// Klipper LPC uses generic/armcm_timer.c (DWT + SysTick), so no
// chip-specific timer modeling is needed. Watchdog (LPC_WDT @
// 0x40000000), GPIO (LPC_GPIO @ 0x2009C000), and other peripheral
// writes go to unmapped addresses and produce harmless log
// warnings; the firmware doesn't read them back to gate progress
// in the printers.test scope.
//
// LPC_SC stub is runtime-injected by the launcher
// (_EXTRA_PERIPHERAL_STUBS_FOR_CHIP['lpc176x']) rather than declared
// here, mirroring the AFEC and SAMD clock-stub paths - keeps the
// stub script path checkout-relative instead of baked into the
// .repl.

cpu: CPU.CortexM @ sysbus
    cpuType: "cortex-m3"
    nvic: nvic

nvic: IRQControllers.NVIC @ sysbus 0xE000E000
    -> cpu@0
    systickFrequency: 100000000

dwt: Miscellaneous.DWT @ sysbus 0xE0001000
    frequency: 100000000

flash: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x0
    size: 0x80000

sram: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x10000000
    size: 0x8000

uart0: UART.NS16550 @ sysbus 0x4000C000
    wideRegisters: true
    ->nvic@5
